This file lists the third-party dependency licences resolved for the release
tarball's binary. It is generated from the workspace's own dependency graph
(`cargo metadata` and `cargo tree -p irontraffic -e normal`), not hand
maintained, so that it cannot silently go stale as dependencies change; see
"How this file is produced and kept current" below.

## Feature set this file describes

Default features (`control-plane`), the feature set the default release
tarball ships. `crates/irontraffic` has no `crypto-fips` build today: the
`crypto-fips` feature belongs to `crates/irontraffic-tls`, and
`crates/irontraffic` (the binary this tarball packages) does not depend on
that crate. `deny.toml`'s accepted OpenSSL licence exception for
`aws-lc-fips-sys` (issue #488) therefore does not enter this binary's
dependency graph under any feature combination it currently has, and the
attribution obligation that exception anticipated does not yet apply to any
artifact this NOTICE describes. When TLS is wired into `crates/irontraffic`
and a `crypto-fips` release artifact becomes buildable, this file must be
regenerated for that feature set specifically and will then need an
`aws-lc-fips-sys` (OpenSSL licence) section; it does not need one today, and
adding one now would be attributing a licence term to a binary that does not
carry it.

